### Project pitfalls (check before coding)

- **Wrong app:** `ucp-dev` vs `ucp-live` — confirm with user if unclear.
- **Commands:** run `php artisan`, `npm`, `pint` from the **app directory**, not monorepo root.
- **Laravel Boost:** prefer Boost MCP tools (`search-docs`, `database-schema`) inside the target app.
- **Legacy:** `app/Support/legacy_functions.php` — reference only; implement in Laravel patterns.
- **Tests:** PHPUnit only (no Pest); run minimal filter after changes.
- **Frontend:** UI not updating → `npm run dev` / `composer run dev` in that app.

### Build & test

```
cd acp   # or ucp-dev / ucp-live
php artisan test --compact --filter=TestName
vendor/bin/pint --dirty --format agent
npm run dev   # or: composer run dev
```

- Test/build only when user says so or fix must be verified.
- `vendor/`, `node_modules/` — never commit.

### Definition of done (per function)

- [ ] Only requested function changed (Golden Rule)
- [ ] Correct app; that app’s `AGENTS.md` followed
- [ ] Affected tests pass (if tests run)
- [ ] Pint run on changed PHP (if PHP changed)
- [ ] Manual check described (route/page/action to verify)

### Git

- **Never commit** unless user explicitly asks.
- No destructive git ops without user approval.

## Communication

- Replies to user: **English or French**, clear and concise (match user language).
- Code/comments/commits: **English** (project convention).

## Stop signals

- Unrequested change → revert / don’t commit.
- Subagent without research at S2+ → stop, run `explore` first.
- Design deviation from existing app patterns → **ask user**.
- Subagent fails → escalate once (S2→S3 model), then ask user.
- Done → short reply, no essay.

